! Extending the editor

!! Toolbar and command menus are different layers

The standard editor toolbar remains the TiddlyWiki presentation and configuration layer. Its `tm-edit-text-operation` messages are adapted to semantic ProseMirror commands in `core/text-operations.js`.

Slash and block menus need a different catalogue: they expose only appropriate toolbar-like actions and also contain structural actions that do not belong in the toolbar. These commands are described by `$:/tags/EditorCommand` tiddlers. The editor-independent `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/editor-command-menu` plugin discovers, filters and displays descriptors, but never mutates an editor document.

Both paths meet at `core/editor-commands.js`. It executes document changes as ProseMirror transactions, preserving selection, history and WikiText source ownership. A command descriptor is configuration, not executable code.

The toolbar adapter covers the core `texteditoroperation` contract as follows:

|!Operation |!Structured behaviour |
|`wrap-selection` |Native marks, links and transclusions; arbitrary wrappers around an existing selection become an exact source-backed inline node |
|`prefix-lines` |Native headings and lists; other prefixes transform complete selected top-level blocks through source-backed WikiText |
|`wrap-lines` |Native code blocks and blockquotes; other wrappers transform complete selected top-level blocks through source-backed WikiText |
|`make-link` |Creates or updates a ProseMirror link mark |
|`insert-text`, `replace-selection` |Parses complete WikiText and inserts structured or source-backed nodes |
|`replace-all` |Parses the replacement and replaces the document through a transaction |
|`excise` |Creates the new tiddler and replaces the structural selection with a link, transclusion or macro |
|`save-selection` |Serialises the structural selection into the requested tiddler field |
|`focus-editor` |Focuses the editor instance |

An unknown operation or an operation that cannot be represented safely is explicitly declined. It must not fall through to the legacy text-offset implementation. In particular, an arbitrary prefix/suffix pair with an empty selection cannot provide a cursor inside unparsed WikiText in visual mode; such a toolbar extension should insert a complete snippet or provide an editor-specific semantic command.

!! Command descriptors

Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/EditorCommand` and give it a semantic `command-id`:

|!Field |!Meaning |
|`command-id` |Required semantic operation handled by the editor adapter |
|`command-key` |Optional stable instance identity; defaults to the descriptor title |
|`caption` |Label, rendered to plain text |
|`description` |Optional secondary text, rendered to plain text |
|`icon` |Optional tiddler containing an SVG icon |
|`command-category` |Grouping key; defaults to `other` |
|`command-surfaces` |Optional list of surfaces such as `slash-menu` or `block-menu` |
|`command-editors` |Optional editor-type list, for example `prosemirror` |
|`command-content-types` |Optional content-type list, for example `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` |
|`command-keywords` |Optional extra search terms |
|other `command-*` fields |Parameters passed to the semantic handler with the prefix removed |

An omitted context-list field is unrestricted. A descriptor that should appear only in this editor should therefore say `command-editors: prosemirror`. Menu ordering first follows the list field of `$:/tags/EditorCommand`, then labels are sorted within each category.

For example:

```
title: $:/Example/EditorCommand/notice
tags: $:/tags/EditorCommand
caption: Insert notice
command-id: insert-notice
command-kind: warning
command-category: block-insert
command-surfaces: slash-menu
command-editors: prosemirror
command-content-types: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
```

!! Implementing a semantic command

Built-in commands live in `core/editor-commands.js`. Plugins can add handlers with a `prosemirroreditorcommand` module. Export a function under the same name as `command-id`:

```
/*\
title: $:/plugins/example/insert-notice.js
type: application/javascript
module-type: prosemirroreditorcommand

\*/

"use strict";

exports["insert-notice"] = function(context, command, execute) {
	var view = context.view;
	if(!view || !view.state.schema.nodes.paragraph) {
		return false;
	}
	if(execute) {
		view.dispatch(view.state.tr.insertText("Notice: ").scrollIntoView());
	}
	return true;
};
```

The third argument is `false` while testing availability and `true` while executing. A handler should return `false` when the current selection or schema cannot support the operation and must not mutate anything during the availability call. Parameters such as `command-kind` are available as `command.parameters.kind`.

Do not convert ProseMirror positions to offsets in the saved WikiText and do not replace the whole editor document merely to run an action. Use a transaction, or return `false` if the operation cannot be expressed safely. New content derived from moved, duplicated or newly constructed nodes must not inherit source-provenance metadata.

!! Snippets

Tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/TextEditor/Snippet` are adapted by the ProseMirror slash-menu plugin into transient `insert-snippet` commands. This compatibility rule is deliberately not part of the generic command registry.

!! Source-safe AST conversion

`ast/` converts between the TiddlyWiki parse tree and the ProseMirror document. Exact original source is attached as provenance to unchanged groups. Unsupported inline and block constructs become `opaque_inline` and `opaque_block` nodes that retain their raw WikiText. Serialisation reuses exact source only while the owning group remains unchanged; structurally edited content is serialised from the current ProseMirror nodes.

An opaque node is reparsed against its own temporary `$:/temp/ProseMirror/RenderedBlock...` tiddler before its preview is rendered. This is important for third-party WikiText rules that record source offsets and later write to `currentTiddler`: their offsets stay local to the opaque node, and a write is converted back into a ProseMirror transaction with normal undo and multi-editor synchronisation. The temporary tiddler copies the source tiddler's fields for rendering context, is removed with the node view and is excluded by the standard saver and sync filters. `currentTiddler` deliberately names the sandbox; the original edited title is available as `prosemirrorSourceTiddler`. A rendered widget must not bypass this bridge to mutate the original tiddler text.

Node views and menu views must create DOM through the owning editor's `ownerDocument`. They must remove listeners, TiddlyWiki widgets, timers and appended menu roots in `destroy()`, so multiple editors and non-global documents remain isolated.

!! Architecture

* `core/` owns the schema, editor engine, shared plugins, keymaps, toolbar adaptation and semantic commands.
* `ast/` owns bidirectional WikiText conversion and source provenance.
* `blocks/` owns source-backed and specialised node views.
* `features/` owns editor interactions such as autocomplete, find/replace, slash menu and drag handle.
* `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/editor-command-menu` owns only reusable descriptor discovery and accessible menu DOM.
